  "compassBuilding": "Building direction",
  "compassNorthBuildingDesc": "For buildings where the magnetic field is disturbed. Draw one line along an outer wall on the map, then just touch the phone to a wall and tap once.",
  "compassNorthBuildingMore": "In modern buildings, steel rebar, electrical boxes, phones and large appliances often deflect the compass needle badly, so true and magnetic north are both off. Building direction uses the building itself: most room walls are parallel or perpendicular to the outer wall. Lay the phone flat with its long edge against any wall and tap “Align to wall”; the compass snaps to the right direction in about a second. The gyroscope holds it for a few minutes after you move away; when it drifts, align again. Save separate places such as Home and Work.",
